lic `SeedData.Run` method is called with `AppDb`. then Each database table contains at least two rows based on contract examples, and every reference between related rows resolves to an existing row.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If `Seed:Demo` is false or unset, the Meridian API shall not run the demo seeder or create demo rows.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A newly created PostgreSQL database and `Seed:Demo` is false or unset. when The API starts. then The demo-table row count is zero.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"If `Seed:Demo` is false and a contract collection operation has no matching database records, the Meridian API shall return an empty list without inserting demo records; whenever a collection operation has no matching persisted records, it shall return an empty list rather than unpersisted sample records.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The configured PostgreSQL database has no matching records for a contract collection operation and `Seed:Demo` is false. when The application starts and a client calls that collection operation. then The database row count remains zero and the response status is 200 with an empty list.\",\n    \"Given A fresh empty database, `Seed:Demo` set to false, and an authorized test caller. when The API starts and each contract list operation is called with filters matching no rows. then Each response status is the contract-declared success status, each returned list count is 0, and the database contains no demo row.\",\n    \"Given A collection operation has no matching database records. when A client calls that operation. then The response status and response list count show a successful empty collection.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall use the existing staff identity provider configured with a deployment-provided authorization URL and token-validation settings, return the configured URL from the contracted authorization-URL operation, and validate staff tokens using those settin